Accept both spellings of the summary status in the client. Do not rely on the server changing, because the format is upstream's documented wire format (runtime_threads.rs:5457).

In src/components/layout/Sidebar.tsx:81, replace `s.latest_turn_status === "in_progress"` with a shared helper:

```ts
const isActiveTurnStatus = (st?: string | null) => {
  const v = (st ?? "").toLowerCase().replace(/[_\- ]/g, "");
  return v === "inprogress" || v === "queued";
};
```

Then use `const running = useThreads((st) => !!st.threads[s.id]?.activeTurnId) || isActiveTurnStatus(s.latest_turn_status);`

Optionally narrow the type in src/lib/types.ts:45 to `"queued" | "inprogress" | "completed" | "failed" | "interrupted" | "canceled" | string | null` and add a comment that this field is Debug-lowercased, unlike turn.status, which is snake_case. Put the helper in src/lib so any other code that reads the summary status uses the same check.

Nothing on the request side needs to change. The `!s.archived` filter is redundant but harmless, since the default filter is active-only (runtime_api.rs:976-986).
